# How far grouped affine quantization moves weights and one output.
#
# Eight weights in two groups of four. At 4 bits with binary16 scales
# and at 8 bits with bfloat16 scales, every weight lies within the
# a-priori error_bound of its group. At 8 bits the bfloat16 scale of
# the first group rounds down, the top of its range falls short of
# 999/1000, and that weight lands further than half a scale from its
# code: the usual "scale / 2" claim is false there, and error_bound is
# attained.
#
# QuantGap is one output of the first group's linear layer, exact
# weights minus the 4-bit read-back (the first weight, 0, is coded
# exactly and left out; the others pinned to dequantize(fit(...))
# below). Over inputs in [-1, 1] the gap ranges over
# [-1351/1024000, 1351/1024000] (itv_dot of the weight differences),
# and both ends are attained at box corners. Run under carrier worlds
# it shows why the affine world exists: interval arithmetic evaluates
# the two dot products apart and encloses about [-4, 4]; the affine
# world keeps the inputs shared and returns 0 ± 1351/1024000, the
# exact range:
#
#   emath compare grouped_error.emath --function QuantGap
#       --set x1=[-1,1] --set x2=[-1,1] --set x3=[-1,1]
#       --world interval --world affine
#
# Run: emath test grouped_error.emath

use fold.reduce
use algebra.linear.spaces
use analysis.intervals
use numerics.floats
use numerics.grouped

emath function QuantGap:
    inputs:
        x1: Rat
        x2: Rat
        x3: Rat
    outputs:
        result: Rat
    definitions:
        y = 1 / 3 * x1 + 2 / 3 * x2 + 999 / 1000 * x3
        yq = 5455 / 16384 * x1 + 5455 / 8192 * x2 + 16365 / 16384 * x3
        result = y - yq

emath function GroupedError:
    inputs:
        unused: Int
    outputs:
        within_bound: Bool
        half_scale_broken: Bool
        bound_attained: Bool
        read_back_pinned: Bool
        gap: Itv
        attained: Bool
    definitions:
        w = [0 / 1, 1 / 3, 2 / 3, 999 / 1000, 0 - 3 / 4, 0 - 1 / 10, 1 / 5, 1 / 2]
        four = fit(binary16(0), 4, 4, w)
        eight = fit(bfloat16(0), 8, 4, w)
        holds = function q in Grouped: all(function j in Int: worst_error(w, q)[j] <= error_bound(w, q)[j], range(0, 2))
        within_bound = holds(four) and holds(eight)
        half_scale_broken = worst_error(w, eight)[0] > eight.grids[0].scale / 2
        bound_attained = worst_error(w, eight)[0] == error_bound(w, eight)[0]
        back = take(dequantize(four), 4)
        read_back_pinned = back == [0 / 1, 5455 / 16384, 5455 / 8192, 16365 / 16384]
        d = vec_add(take(w, 4), vec_scale(0 - 1 / 1, back))
        gap = itv_dot(d, repeat(Itv: {lo: 0 - 1 / 1, hi: 1 / 1}, 4))
        corner = function up in Bool: map(function di in Rat: if (di >= 0 / 1) == up: 1 / 1 else: 0 - 1 / 1, d)
        attained = vec_dot(d, corner(true)) == gap.hi and vec_dot(d, corner(false)) == gap.lo
    tests:
        example <grouped_error>:
            given unused = 0
            expect within_bound == true
            expect half_scale_broken == true
            expect bound_attained == true
            expect read_back_pinned == true
            expect gap == Itv: {lo: 0 - 1351 / 1024000, hi: 1351 / 1024000}
            expect attained == true
